  "problem": "The battery charge of a delivery drone, measured in percent, is given by the function $B(t)$, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since the drone was fully charged. The values of $B(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $B(t)$ | $80$ | $72$ | $55$ | $40$ | $35$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of the battery charge when $t=6$ using a backward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\nThe estimated rate of change when $t=6$ is\n{{field-1}} percent per hour.",
